			<div class="content" id="post-content-2400983">
									

<p>+1</p>
<p>I love this cute little civilization, getting scared of lice and overbreeding during turmoil, causing a little mini explosion, worshiping the grain of rice, and then flying the WiFi dongle away. :p</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Bad&nbsp;Stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Anyways, I was a bit confused at the beginning description, and throughout some of the descriptions of events. I think it could be cleaned up and smoothed a bit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The explosion obliterates SCP-2978-24 and damages 3 additional communities, causing ████ SCPX-2978-B deaths.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What's SCPX? Is that a typo?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All communities are named &quot;Motherburg&quot;, with the suffix &quot;V1.x&quot; added to each new iteration. On all SCP-2978-A instances, the following will be printed on an upright transistor, located near the edge of the motherboard: &quot;Welcome to Motherburg, Population:(variable)&quot;. As of 04/10/20██, &quot;Motherburg V1.██&quot; is the last community to have been built.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So wait, is there one civilization across multiple motherboards, or multiple motherboards with multiple civilizations??</p>
<p>There's also a lot of SCP-2978-24, SCP-2978-B, SCP-2978-dsfhjk repetitions which sometimes make it difficult to read. Consider consolidating them into things like, &quot;the affected region,&quot; or &quot;the population,&quot; or &quot;the motherboard.&quot;</p>
<p>Finally, I think the SCP foundation could contain a flying wireless router moving at 18&#160;km/h.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Great job! I like this one a lot!</p>

							</div>

								
